Once upon a time I was a nethack addict--game after game, learning a lot of
tactics & strategies, but never quite able to FINISH the @$&@$^& thing.  Then
I discovered Explore mode.  Now I could finish the game, and the WoW to start
with was pretty cool too.  But I lusted for more.  More power.  -127 AC.  HP
in the thousands.  25/25/18/25/25/25 ability scores.  Artifacts galore.

And so I downloaded nethack binaries onto a PC and after too long, I COULD
PLAY DEBUG MODE!!!!  AAAAAHAHAHAHAHAHA!!!!  Unlimited wishes!  Auto level
mapping!  Special level locations revealed to me!

Well, needless to say I doubt I'll be playing regular nethack anytime soon
(high score list doesn't really appeal to me) and even Explore mode has lost
its appeal.  Why settle for less when you can have absolute power?

I figure another week or two of playing, before debug mode loses its novelty.
Then I'll be free!!  Freed from the addictive enslavement this game has
wrought upon me....
